docs\reports\P9-EXE.md-194-
docs\reports\P9-EXE.md-195-- **No person has started it or looked at its live window.** The nearest test was the build copied to `%TEMP%\tl exe manual\Third Life\` and started with `explorer.exe "<exe>"`: parent process explorer, no arguments. After 10 s the window "Third Life" was responding, and the PowerShell helper was a child with window handle 0. The close message ended the process by itself, its log ends with `[tl] world done`, and nothing was left. That window appeared on the desktop for about 11 s, twice.
docs\reports\P9-EXE.md-196-- **Steering by hand,** the feel of the camera, and playing a game with real keys.
docs\reports\P9-EXE.md-197-- **Entering by keys** was done only for the paddle court. The hockey rink, track and wall yard were entered only by the scripted tour.
docs\reports\P9-EXE.md-198-- **The message box** for a failed start is written but was not seen. The same refusal was tested headless: log line, exit 2.
docs\reports\P9-EXE.md-199-- **Sound,** other machines, SmartScreen and antivirus.
docs\reports\P9-EXE.md:200:- **The merged tree.** If another builder changes `view.gd` or `world.gd` (`start(options)`, or the properties `world`, `draw`, `stage`, `visitor`, `player_pos`, `_ended`, `_end()`), `boot.gd` must follow. The check will say so.
docs\reports\P9-EXE.md-201-- **A Jolt warning** ("job system exceeded the maximum number of jobs") printed in two of three editor-binary windows with seven games. It did not appear in the exe's logs.
docs\reports\P9-EXE.md-202-
docs\reports\P9-EXE.md-203-QUESTIONS
docs\reports\P9-EXE.md-204-
docs\reports\P9-EXE.md-205-1. Should the build's identity line be a contract (a `tl.`-prefixed schema in `contracts/`)? I used `thirdlife.exe/1` to keep the gate green without touching contracts.
docs\reports\P9-EXE.md-206-2. Should the exe have its own user data folder? It shares `Third Life Engine` with every dev process. That needs more `project.godot` lines than the one I was allowed.
docs\reports\P9-EXE.md-207-3. Is radius 46 for the hockey plot acceptable until `edge_height` is fixed (patch 5)?
