docs\reports\P4-RELIEF.md-46-**5. A body for the visitor.**
docs\reports\P4-RELIEF.md-47-- What I chose: the world owns a `PhysicsServer3D` space, built once with the landscape. It holds only static things:
docs\reports\P4-RELIEF.md-48-  - the terrain triangles, left out where a plot's own ground carries him;
docs\reports\P4-RELIEF.md-49-  - a wall along every fence with the gate open, tree and rock trunks, the lots' machinery, and the bridge;
docs\reports\P4-RELIEF.md-50-  - a **copy of every pack's static colliders**, clipped to the plot circle and bent at the rim the way the draw layer bends the ground.
docs\reports\P4-RELIEF.md-51-- The pack's shapes are shared (a shape belongs to no space), but the bodies are new ones in the world's space. Pack bodies are never touched.
docs\reports\P4-RELIEF.md-52-- His body is a kinematic capsule moved with `test_motion`. It steps up 0.55 m, slides along obstacles, and refuses slopes over 55°.
docs\reports\P4-RELIEF.md:53:- The scheduler still reads the scripted `player_pos`, so the proof is unchanged. The body only decides where he is drawn. When a person walks (`--live`), the body sets `player_pos`.
docs\reports\P4-RELIEF.md-54-- Probes (`walks/visitor_walk.json`, `world.sh tour visitor_walk ...`): 8 of 8 behave as expected.
