engine\kernel\world\terrain\world_body.gd-2-## Walker-feel (lane M, 18 Nov 2026): the body of a person's visitor, with weight. It moves the world's kinematic
engine\kernel\world\terrain\world_body.gd-3-## capsule (terrain/world_space.gd, `sp`) by VELOCITY, one `drive()` per world tick (60 Hz; every number below is per
engine\kernel\world\terrain\world_body.gd-4-## second or counted in ticks). `world_space.gd walk()` stays for the probes and a scripted walk.
engine\kernel\world\terrain\world_body.gd:5:##   ground   the horizontal velocity eases toward the wish: ACCEL m/s^2 while the wish has a direction, DECEL while it
engine\kernel\world\terrain\world_body.gd-6-##            is let go; standing still on walkable ground is not a move at all (no test, no creep).
engine\kernel\world\terrain\world_body.gd-7-##   air      gravity GRAVITY, falls at most FALL_MAX; a little steering (AIR_ACCEL); lands on walkable ground.
engine\kernel\world\terrain\world_body.gd-8-##   jump     JUMP_V up (h = JUMP_V^2 / 2g = 1.0 m, about 35 ticks in the air on flat ground); allowed COYOTE ticks
engine\kernel\world\terrain\world_body.gd-9-##            after walking off an edge; a press is kept BUFFER ticks, so a press just before landing still jumps.
engine\kernel\world\terrain\world_body.gd-10-##   slope    ground steeper than `max_slope_deg`: he slides down it, gaining speed along it (gravity projected on the
engine\kernel\world\terrain\world_body.gd-11-##            slope, SLOPE_FRICTION against it, at most SLOPE_MAX), steerable a little (SLOPE_STEER), until he stands on
engine\kernel\world\terrain\world_body.gd-12-##            walkable ground again. Walking UP into such ground is refused as before (a wall); walking DOWN onto it
--
